Z||000062||Ken Wittlief||10-25-2001||09:23 PM||||I hate<BR>little baby ducks<BR>old pickup trucks<BR>walking in the rain<BR>and pain.<P> oh wait, this was suppose to be about inventions :c)<P> answering machines - is there anything worst than calling long distance and a machine answers, now you have to pay for the LD call, and you still dont get to talk to the person.<P> caller ID - just pick up the phone already<P> microwave ovens - half the stuff you want to heat up in there either explodes (beans, chili, meatballs) or it comes out limp and soggy (pizza, dougnuts, pretzils) or it starts on fire and creates a foul stench that lingers for hours (popcorn)<BR> <BR> Cars: I love driving my cars but I absolutely HATE the way they are built and the way they are put together - I could design an outstanding electric vehicle if I had the capitol to produce it. An internal combustion engine is a mechanical NIGHTMARE!<P> Computers: Its not really the computer itself, its the dam SW - starting with the operating system and including just about every program and application on the market. I have a $1,200 PIII computer upstairs that nobody can use cause it crashes every 20 minutes. To wipe the HD and reinstall all the programs would take about 20 hours of work.<P> air conditioning: I would rather sit by a window fan on a hot summers nite than be in an air conditioned room, with the humidity at 4%, your sinuses all dried out, that nasty stale musty AC smell, and that constant droning - you know the noise - im not sure if its the compressor motor or the sound of the electric meter spinning like crazy on the side of the house.<P> Florescent lights: I can see them flicker - maybe my persistance of vision is not as long as most peoples but I find them very annoying and stressful - for me its like sitting in a room with a disco strobe light.<P> clocks: I hate the fact that we live in a world where we are controlled by a stupid little machine on the wall - it tells us when to get up, when to goto work, when to eat, when to go home - I would much rather live in a world where you get up when you wake up, eat when you are hungry, goto work when you feel productive, and have sex whenever you damwell feel like it [i had to throw that in for anyone that read this whole long post :c]||||reg||1
